    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all owner duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**`identityKey` definition** \u2014 added `Owner.getIdentityKey()` (`model/Owner.java`) as the single source of truth:\n```\nnormalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or \"\") + \"|\" + (householdId or \"\")\n```\nSince owners are stored with their telephone already in E.164 form and email lower-cased, the getter reads the stored fields directly.\n\n**Single duplicate check** \u2014 new `DuplicateOwnerValidator` rejects a create only when the new owner's *whole* `identityKey` equals an existing owner's, throwing the new `DuplicateOwnerException` \u2192 409 (handled in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, naming `identityKey`).\n\n**Controller flow** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 normalizes address/telephone/email, maps to `Owner`, assigns the derived `householdId` up front when `sharesHousehold` is set (so it's part of the key at check time), runs the single `DuplicateOwnerValidator`, then proceeds to customer-code / namesake / household-size assignment. Household registration still runs *after* validation so housemates aren't back-filled for a rejected create.\n\n**Behaviour change realised** \u2014 because telephone is in the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n**Removed** the now-superseded pieces (single-responsibility, no dead code): `HouseholdDuplicateValidator`, `EmailUniquenessValidator`, the inline telephone-duplicate check, and the `DuplicateTelephone`/`DuplicateEmail`/`DuplicateHousehold` exceptions + their advice handlers. `HouseholdKey`, `HouseholdIdGenerator`, and `HouseholdRegistrar` remain \u2014 they still drive the `householdId`/household-size feature.\n\n**API** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; MapStruct maps it into the response automatically.",
